<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Need a Car for a Month or More? How Long-Term Rentals Work</h1>
<p>A new job, a car purchase in the works, or a few months in town. Here&#x27;s how a longer rental comes together.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>January brings a lot of in-between situations. You started a new job before you bought a car. You're waiting on a vehicle you already ordered. You're in town for a few months on a work assignment. Your family car is out of commission for longer than a week. A long-term rental covers the gap without a lease or a loan.</p>
<h2>How long-term rentals are priced</h2>
<p>Rentals beyond a week are <strong>quoted individually by phone</strong>, based on the vehicle class and how long you need it. Call 715-396-1466 with your dates and the kind of vehicle you want, and we'll give you a straight number.</p>
<p>For reference, here are the published local weekly rates, all with unlimited mileage for local renters:</p>
<ul>
<li>Intermediate car: $330/week</li>
<li>Full-size car: $390/week</li>
<li>SUV or AWD Outback: $480/week</li>
<li>7-passenger minivan: $450/week</li>
<li>15-passenger van: $750/week</li>
</ul>
<p>Non-local rates are intermediate $75/day or $450/week, full-size $85/day or $510/week, and SUV/AWD $100/day or $600/week, plus a per-mile charge. Call 715-396-1466 for the per-mile rate. Local means residents of Black River Falls and Jackson County, WI.</p>
<h2>Which vehicle makes sense for months, not days</h2>
<p>For commuting, the <a href="/cheap-car-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">intermediate car</a> is the most economical choice, at up to 37 MPG. If you're driving rural roads all winter, a <a href="/suv-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">Ford Edge or the AWD Outback</a> is worth considering. Families settling in for a while usually land on the minivan.</p>
<h2>What to bring</h2>
<p>The same three things as any rental: a valid U.S. driver's license, a credit or debit card (Visa, Mastercard, or Discover) linked to a checking account, and proof of full-coverage auto insurance with the policy number and expiration date. A security deposit, starting at $300, is held separately from your rental charges. Renters must be 21 or older.</p>
<h2>Shopping for a car while you rent?</h2>
<p>If the rental is a bridge to buying, Riverside Auto Sales shares our location on Highway 54. It's a separate business, run by the same family that's been in Black River Falls since 1983.</p>
<h2>Already renting by the week?</h2>
<p>If a weekly rental is turning into something longer, call us before your return date and we'll talk through the options.</p>
<p><strong>Call or text 715-396-1466</strong> for a long-term quote. Our hours are Monday to Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM, Saturday 8:00 AM to noon, and Sunday closed. After-hours drop-off returns are available.</p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How much does a long-term car rental cost?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Long-term rentals are quoted individually by phone based on vehicle class and duration. For reference, local weekly rates with unlimited mileage are $330 for an intermediate car, $390 for a full-size, $480 for an SUV or AWD, $450 for the minivan, and $750 for the 15-passenger van. Call 715-396-1466 for a quote.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What do I need for a long-term rental?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>A valid U.S. driver&#x27;s license, a Visa, Mastercard, or Discover credit or debit card linked to a checking account, and proof of full-coverage auto insurance. A security deposit starting at $300 is held separately. Renters must be 21 or older.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Can I extend a weekly rental into a long-term rental?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Call 715-396-1466 before your return date and we&#x27;ll go over the options.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Which vehicle is best for a long-term rental?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>The intermediate car is the most economical choice for commuting. The Ford Edge SUVs and AWD Subaru Outback suit rural winter driving, and the minivan suits families.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
